Third-party data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The metro station, line, and coordinate data under data/ (including
data/systems/ and data/gtfs/) is derived from two kinds of public source:

1. Transit-agency GTFS feeds and official agency information, for fares,
   operating hours, station lists, and line topology:
     - MARTA, Atlanta (itsmarta.com)
     - Doha Metro, Qatar
     - BART, San Francisco Bay Area (bart.gov)
     - Taipei MRT (metro.taipei)
     - Chicago CTA "L" (transitchicago.com, chicago-l.org)
     - Beijing Subway
   Factual data such as fares, operating hours, and policies reflects public
   agency information as of the dates noted in docs/references.md.

2. Wikipedia / Wikimedia, for station lists, geographic coordinates, and line
   topology (notably the files data/gtfs/*_wiki.json and *_scraped.json, and
   the per-station coordinates used by data/verify.py).

   Wikipedia content is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 by its respective authors. The
   Wikipedia-derived portions of this dataset are redistributed under
   CC BY-SA 4.0, with attribution to the Wikipedia contributors of the
   corresponding metro-system articles. The CC BY-SA 4.0 license text is at
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.

